completions_2:
First, find the number of friends Amy has. Amy made 20 more friends than Lily, and Lily made 50 friends. Therefore, Amy made 50 + 20 = 70 friends.

Next, find the total number of friends Lily and Amy have together. Lily made 50 friends and Amy made 70 friends, so together they have 50 + 70 = 120 friends.

\boxed{120}

completions_4:
20. [Total Points: 10]

Violetta wants 5 crayons, and each crayon costs $2. So the total cost of the crayons will be 5 * $2 = $10.  She has $20 and spends $10. Therefore, her change will be $20 - $10 = $10.

\boxed{10}
